---
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Responsible Gambling — Casilla"
  description="Practical limits worth setting before you deposit, the warning signs that matter, and where to get free confidential help."
>
  <h1 class="text-[32px] sm:text-[38px]">Responsible gambling</h1>

  <Prose>
    <p class="mt-5">
      This site compares gambling operators, so it would be dishonest to skip the part where
      we say that gambling loses most people money most of the time. The house edge is not a
      rumour — it is the arithmetic the entire industry is built on, and no strategy, bonus
      or provably fair algorithm changes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you deposit</h2>
    <p>
      Decide the amount you are prepared to lose entirely, and treat it as the price of an
      evening rather than an investment that might come back. Set the deposit limit in your
      account before you play, not after a bad session, because the moment you most want the
      limit is the moment you will least want to set it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Crypto adds two specific risks worth naming. Deposits are effectively irreversible, so
      there is no chargeback and no bank to intervene. And a balance denominated in a
      volatile asset makes it genuinely hard to feel how much real money is on the table.
    </p>

    <h2>Signs it has stopped being entertainment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Chasing losses — depositing again specifically to win back what just went</li>
      <li>Gambling with money meant for something else</li>
      <li>Hiding how much you play, or how much you have lost, from people close to you</li>
      <li>Borrowing to keep playing</li>
      <li>Feeling you cannot stop, or feeling worse rather than better afterwards</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where to get help</h2>
    <p>
      These services are free, confidential, and independent of any operator.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.begambleaware.org/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"
          >BeGambleAware</a
        > — advice and a free national helpline
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.gamcare.org.uk/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">GamCare</a
        > — support, live chat and treatment referral
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.gamblingtherapy.org/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"
          >Gambling Therapy</a
        > — free support in multiple languages, worldwide
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.gamblersanonymous.org/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"
          >Gamblers Anonymous</a
        > — peer support meetings, online and in person
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Blocking software</h2>
    <p>
      If you want the decision taken out of your hands, tools like Gamban and BetBlocker
      block gambling sites across your devices, including crypto casinos that self-exclusion
      registers do not cover. BetBlocker is free.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>You must be 18 or older</strong> to gamble, and older in some jurisdictions.
      Casilla is not a gambling operator, holds no licence, and takes no bets.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
